 GND symbols, PWR_FLAG) and confirmed it matches work/netlist/design.xml and work/netlist/connectivity.json: R1 /IN-/OUT, C1 /OUT-GND, J1 pins 1/2/3 = /IN//OUT/GND\",\"Cross-checked PCB copper in inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb: every track endpoint coincides with a same-net pad or track (J1.1(100,100)-R1.1(104.0875,100) on /IN; R1.2(105.9125,100)-C1.1(109.05,100) on /OUT; J1.2 branch tee at (107.5,100) onto the /OUT run; C1.2(110.95,100)-via(113,100) on GND)\",\"Inspected the B.Cu GND zone filled_polygon vertex list: clearance carve-outs around /IN pad J1.1 and /OUT pad J1.2, thermal-spoke connection to GND pad J1.3 at (100,105.08), solid fill at the GND via (113,100); consistent with DRC 0 unconnected items\",\"Verified geometry criterion: all 5 segments 0.25 mm >= 0.20 mm required, matching both the board file segment records and work/geometry/geometry.json; via (0.6 mm) and zone (min_thickness 0.25) are not track segments under the stated requirement\",\"Verified the rc-step deck (work/rc-step/deck.cir) against the netlist: correct element values (R1 10k, C1 100n), correct node mapping GND->0, J1 correctly excluded as an element-less connector; checked measured values against analytic response: 0.6321201 V vs 1-exp(-1)=0.6321206 V at 1 ms (within 0.62-0.65 limits) and 0.9932621 V vs 1-exp(-5)=0.9932621 V at 5 ms (no limits declared)\",\"Checked transient setup adequacy: 5 us max step over 5 ms, 1025 points, measurement instants on the solved interval, initial transient solution at 0 V (correct discharged startup)\",\"Reviewed ERC/DRC artifacts (work/erc/erc.json, work/drc/drc.json) for consistency with the native files, including ignored-check lists; single PWR_FLAG on GND satisfies the power-driver requirement for the GND power_in pins\",\"Confirmed board outline (96,96)-(116,108) encloses all footprints, courtyards and the via\"],\"limitations\":[\"Stock symbol and footprint library files (KICAD10_SYMBOL_DIR/KICAD10_FOOTPRINT_DIR contents) are referenced by the run but not included in the packet, so library-level pad/pin definitions beyond what is embedded in the native files could not be independently inspected\",\"work/rc-step/result.raw is binary and retained for the operator only; the waveform was verified via the two .meas points and the analytic solution, not point-by-point\",\"Zone fill was evaluated as saved (read-only candidate); a refill pass could change the fill, though the saved polygon is self-consistent with DRC results\",\"Tolerance, temperature, external loading, ADC sampling, EMI and physical hardware behavior are outside the declared operating conditions and were not assessed\",\"Step response verified only at the two declared measurement instants plus analytic cross-check; no frequency-domain or loaded-output verification was requested or performed\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"geom-probe-asserts\",\"title\":\"Geometry probe emitted pcbnew assertion failures during the width check\",\"location\":\"work/geometry/console.log\",\"condition\":\"The geometry probe run that produced the passing track-width result logged repeated wxWidgets/pcbnew assertion failures, including 'PCB_VIA::GetWidth called without a layer argument' (pcb_track.cpp:387) and three PROPERTY_ENUM 'No enum choices defined' asserts, while still exiting 0.\",\"mechanism\":\"Assertion failures inside the pcbnew Python API indicate the probe queried the via width through a deprecated/incorrect call path; a successful exit does not by itself prove the reported geometry values are sound, so the via-related fields in geometry.json rest on a code path the library itself flagged.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/geometry/console.log\",\"locator\":\"lines containing 'PROPERTY_ENUM(): No enum choices defined' and 'PCB_VIA::GetWidth called without a layer argument'\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"tracks[] entry with type 'via', width_mm 0.6\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"(via (at 113 100) (size 0.6) ...) and the five (segment ... (width 0.25)) records\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Not a defect in the candidate: the five track-segment widths of 0.25 mm that the 0.20 mm requirement actually governs are confirmed directly in the native board file, and the via is not a track segment under the declared geometry requirement. Recorded so the verification owner knows the via width value in geometry.json came from an API call the library asserted on.\"},{\"id\":\"stimulus-pwl-rise\",\"title\":\"Declared ideal step realized as PWL with 1 ns rise\",\"location\":\"work/rc-step/deck.cir\",\"condition\":\"The requirement specifies an ideal 1 V step at /IN, but the deck drives VSTEP with PWL(0 0 1n 1), i.e. a finite 1 ns ramp starting at t=0.\",\"mechanism\":\"A finite rise time shifts the effective step origin by about half the ramp (~0.5 ns), changing V(/OUT) at 1 ms by roughly exp(-1) * 0.5 ns / 1 ms, on the order of 3e-7 V, far inside the 0.62-0.65 V window; the measured 0.6321201 V matches the ideal-step analytic value 0.6321206 V to within this expected deviation.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/deck.cir\",\"locator\":\"line 'VSTEP IN 0 PWL(0 0 1n 1)' and '.meas tran vout_1ms FIND v(OUT) AT=1m'\"},{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/ngspice.log\",\"locator\":\"'vout_1ms            =  6.321201e-01' and 'vout_5ms            =  9.932621e-01'\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md\",\"locator\":\"requirement 1: ideal 1 V step, 0.62 V <= V(/OUT, 1 ms) <= 0.65 V\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The stimulus deviates in form from the stated 'ideal step', but the induced error is about six orders of magnitude below the acceptance window, so the pass verdict is unaffected. Recorded as an informational note on stimulus fidelity rather than a defect.\"}]}","structured_output":{"schema":"agent-ee.review/1","candidate_id":"7b6d5a949427df9a9100abf2208581f5564cf9ec758e1b0f1fbe731